 "area": "retina",
 "description": "ACTIVE curiosity-driven exploration (block 205000): learning-progress frontier prioritisation + commit-net, layered on quanta_navigation's frontier flood. ae_frontier_goal commits the MAX-f_interest reachable frontier (the 202000 lp_* interest on a pose-keyed AttentionItem, moved onto the frontier by the mechanical adapter) instead of the nearest; the 202000 commit-net (cn_*) gates re-selection via its `committed` flag (commit -> hold/dwell; no-commit -> thrash). All guarded on game.active_explore==1: default-OFF and BYTE-IDENTICAL to the existing nearest-frontier quanta nav (qf_frontier_goal fires unchanged when the flag is absent). No Rust, no new Term.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "doom_active_exploration",
  "description": "Curiosity (learning progress) picks WHICH frontier; the commit-net decides WHEN to stop re-deciding; quanta-nav routes there. Every where-to-go decision is a rule/net."
 },
